      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-8plus2-denomix-r2v.jpg",
      "description": "Put your people, places or props into a new shot at 768p with sound. Use this card when you want a steady camera, low-key natural light and textured skin, and a 5 s clip in about 3 minutes on 12 GB.\n\nHOW TO PROMPT. Attach one reference picture for each person, in the order they appear in the prompt. Write the Ref2VA format: subject_definitions, summary, retention_analysis, detailed_description, overall_soundscape and non_diegetic_music. Refer to pictures as <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>, and put spoken lines inside <d>[English] ...</d> tags. Say when the lips close and what happens for the rest of the shot, or H3 fills the time with words you did not write. The card adds no words and no trigger of its own.\n\nWHAT TO EXPECT. DenoMix sits between stock H3 and Singularity v2: less action than v2, a darker picture than stock. In wide shots it often frames people larger than you asked for. Ambience is quiet unless the prompt names the sounds it wants.\n\nSIZES. 768p at 5 s is the tested default for 12 GB. 928p adds real fine detail and is meant for 16 GB or more. A 12 GB card can run 928p or a 10 s clip, but each takes 4 to 20 minutes instead of 3, so close other programs that use the GPU first. Your own LoRAs apply to both passes.\n\nModel format: int8 ConvRot.",
